    "done_when": "Implement section 22 of docs/plans/local-lane-admission-control.html as written there. In imas_ambix/agent/router.py the admission ledger records each admitted request's coordinator session beside its run id (both from identity_from_headers; a run with no session is grouped as session unattributed). A session is working while it has a request in flight or one admitted within WORKING_HORIZON_SECONDS = 180.0. Its workers u are the distinct run ids it has in flight or admitted within that horizon. Capacity C = floor(effective_width / published requests_per_run). With N working sessions, N <= 1 gives the working session the global worker_slots and fair_share C. N >= 2 gives F = floor(C / N), and each session gets max(0, min(G, max(max(0, F - u), G - reserve))), where reserve sums min(max(0, F - u_o), 2) over the other working sessions and G is the global worker_slots. A session not yet working is computed as one extra session with u = 0 and N + 1 sessions. The admission object publishes active_sessions, fair_share, borrow_reserve (2), new_session_worker_slots and sessions {session: {live_runs, worker_slots}}. All are null when requests_per_run is null, and per-session figures are 0 when the verdict is congested, full or paused. imas_ambix/agent/live_panel.py copies those five fields into lane.worker_slots, copying only fields the router published. Tests in tests/test_agent_router_worker_slots.py, at effective width 12 and a published ratio 0.5 (C = 24), assert: one working session with 10 workers is offered the global figure; with A at 2 workers, B at 12 and global worker_slots 10, A is offered 10, B 8 and a new session 8; a session last admitted 200 s ago with nothing in flight stops counting, so the other is offered the global figure; session-less runs form one unattributed session; a congested verdict gives every per-session figure 0. tests/test_live_panel.py asserts the copy. Gate: uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_agent_router_worker_slots.py tests/test_agent_router_admission.py tests/test_agent_router_lane_publish.py tests/test_live_panel.py tests/test_agent_watch_live.py passes, pytest tests/test_agent_serve_registry.py -k agent_package_modules_parse_with_serving_python passes, uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0; the gate log's first line names the commit it ran at and each command's exit status is recorded as EXIT=0 or the non-zero status; any evidence fragment written ends with a trailing newline",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Make the router publish each working session's fair share of worker slots, giving a session working alone the whole server",
